  "comments": {
    "bugs": {
      "19215": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "bug_id": 19215,
            "text": "parse(keep.source = TRUE) can loop forever in finalizeData() when a\nprevious parse in the same session died with a lexer error. Found by\nOSS-Fuzz (testcase 5381026965422080); the hang is in the C code, so it\ncannot be interrupted.\n\nReproducible example (R-devel r90672, from the console; both parses must\nbe in one top-level expression, see below):\n\nlocal({\n    try(parse(text = \"#a\\n#a\\n#a\\ny + '\\\\q'\", keep.source = TRUE), silent = TRUE)\n    parse(text = \"c#\\nc#\\n\", keep.source = TRUE)\n})\n\nObserved: the second parse() never returns. Expected: it returns the\ntwo expressions.\n\nAnalysis:\n\nR_FinalizeSrcRefState() in src/main/gram.y clears the ID_ID/ID_PARENT\nrecords a parse wrote, so that the next parse can reuse the arrays, but\nit loops over 0..identifier-1 while 'identifier' is the id of the last\nnode, not a count. When a lexer error unwinds out of a parse\nmid-expression, that last node is a recorded one, and its ID_ID entry\nsurvives into the next parse. If the same id then lands on an unrecorded\nnode there (expr_or_assign_or_help, prog), finalizeData() takes it for a\nnode present in the parse data: the walk that attaches a comment to its\nenclosing node reaches that node, jumps to the stale row, whose parent\nchain leads back to the node, and cycles.\n\nThe wrapper matters because the console REPL's own parse of the next\ninput line clears ids up to its token count. Rscript and R -f are not\naffected at all: R_ReplFile() keeps the parser state busy for the whole\nfile, so every nested parse() gets fresh arrays. Interactive sessions and\nC callers that evaluate repeatedly (the fuzz harness) reuse them.\n\nProposed patch: attached as parse-data-stale-id.diff. It makes the\ncleanup loop inclusive (0..identifier), in gram.y and the checked-in\ngram.c, and adds a regression test to tests/reg-tests-1e.R. make check\npasses.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/378,\nwhere CI results can be seen.",
            "count": 0,
